# Netlify Redirects — Haus Fund (haus.fund)

# Redirect www to apex
https://www.haus.fund/* https://haus.fund/:splat 301!
https://www.haus.fund https://haus.fund 301!

# Internal docs live in the repo for reference but must not be served.
# publish = "." means every committed file is otherwise reachable.
#
# These must be listed one per file and forced with "!". A wildcard does not
# work here: Netlify only allows a splat at the END of a path, so "/*.md" never
# matches, and without "!" an existing static file wins over the redirect.
#
# ADDING A NEW .md TO THIS REPO? Add a line here too, or it goes live.
/README.md /index.html 404!
/DEPLOYMENT.md /index.html 404!
/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md /index.html 404!
/SKILL.md /index.html 404!
/CONNECT-GIT.md /index.html 404!

# Real files (design-system.html, expansion.html, fund-portal/, assets/) are
# served before this rule. Catch-all sends unknown paths to the homepage.
/* /index.html 200
